+*Figure: An owner stands at the left tossing coins, each one a minute, from a day of 2 h 9 min online, a little under the 141-minute average. The first two coins land on a scrolling feed, a conveyor belt of cards that carries them away toward the edge; nothing comes back, and this lane, labelled Scrolling, fades. The next four coins go into four slot machines labelled Solving, and each pays out one thing into its tray: a worker, a vetted tool, a speech bubble of advice and a gear for a task automated.*
+
 That was my first realization: they're not online for entertainment. They're online to work.
 
